  <data key="d5">1780000501</data>
</node>
<node id="[PERSON] EZ-2">
  <data key="d0">[PERSON] EZ-2</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">EZ-2 is a U.S. Border Patrol/CBP officer based out of El Paso who was identified by Unraveled as Michael Sveum. He was described as wearing a BORTAC vest and as an identified agent linked through reporting by Bellingcat and Evident Media, including lockscreen and social media image comparisons.

EZ-2 was reported as being present during enforcement actions in Minnesota, including outside Roosevelt High School in Minneapolis, where he was involved in use of force against protesters. He was also described as accompanying Bovino on raids in Minnesota, appearing with Bovino and Hewson, and being frequently seen beside EZ-17 in Jan. 7 footage. In these incidents, he was associated with the truck confrontation, less-lethal force deployment, physically pushing protesters to the ground, using a chemical irritant/OC spray, and deploying tear gas, including a tear gas grenade. One description also noted that EZ-2 was hit by a snowball.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48865492ff6980fba6505562f4fd8f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d17e0f591005ffb59a7f371310e5a906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4170a826ce256ee580815639136542ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b93e00a9cc3c6ea937c6c587abe580f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48ffeb8cda0384416cef68fda1fa6092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fef9d4f066439678dcf9e73935433d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a6774ff001e7c0d324470176c02f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d313e963f5afd4511121b3011aa2c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-791d993b170dda54c1f646cc730be410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9817d6c2a44499a793919afdc362415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c623b1d6b3fdbe8556f7ed5defe698b</data>
  <data key="d4">raw/84d7e0b9-ebfc-4681-b2ae-7048a4704aa1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;raw/c1731560-2392-47fb-814c-5a1da0d7084b.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1779999299</data>
</node>
<node id="[PERSON] EZ-17">
  <data key="d0">[PERSON] EZ-17</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">EZ-17 is a Border Patrol officer and masked federal agent based out of El Paso, identifiable by the uniform number patch EZ-17 and described as wearing a BORTAC vest. He is characterized as an elite Border Patrol officer and was identified by multiple sources, including Unraveled, Bellingcat, and Evident Media, with identification supported through vehicle-interior footage and a Facebook image comparison. One description also names him as Edgar Vazquez.

EZ-17 was involved in several law-enforcement actions captured on video. He was seen firing less lethal munitions, including multiple shots and launcher use, passing a tear gas canister to Bovino, and moving alongside other agents. He was also described as physically pushing protesters, reloading, and standing inside the crime scene tape perimeter near Bovino.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48865492ff6980fba6505562f4fd8f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d17e0f591005ffb59a7f371310e5a906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4170a826ce256ee580815639136542ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b93e00a9cc3c6ea937c6c587abe580f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48ffeb8cda0384416cef68fda1fa6092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a6774ff001e7c0d324470176c02f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d313e963f5afd4511121b3011aa2c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-791d993b170dda54c1f646cc730be410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9817d6c2a44499a793919afdc362415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c623b1d6b3fdbe8556f7ed5defe698b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-430166eda1140532dd1c88ca903c35b2</data>
