<node id="[ORGANIZATION] DHS">
  <data key="d0">[ORGANIZATION] DHS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">DHS refers to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security, a federal department referenced in policy, reporting, and incident contexts. It is described as the source of policy guidance, including use-of-force policy guidance, and as being associated with questions about DHS policies and incidents.

In the provided descriptions, DHS is also portrayed as a public-facing authority on law-enforcement actions. It was contacted by Bellingcat, CalMatters, and Evident Media before publication, but had not responded to requests for comment at the time of publication; other descriptions similarly state that DHS did not respond to questions about Vazquez, Sveum, and use-of-force policies, and was otherwise nonresponsive. One description notes that DHS later provided a response after publication. DHS is also linked to public statements and social media activity concerning law-enforcement incidents, including an ICE operation and the Dallas shooting, where it is said to have spoken about the operation, posted on X, published a video, and made statements about the incidents. Additional references say DHS identified Isabel Mata and made a Facebook claim about chemical munitions, and that a DHS officer in footage directly identified the department.

DHS is further described as defending its enforcement practices and use of force. It stated that it was taking reasonable and constitutional measures to uphold the rule of law and protect its officers, and it repeatedly defended the use of riot-control weapons in protests. Specific actions attributed to DHS agents include using 40mm launchers to fire less-lethal munitions, using handheld chemical irritant sprays, and using ECWs in immigration-related raids.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48865492ff6980fba6505562f4fd8f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d17e0f591005ffb59a7f371310e5a906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-144039d9b499b5a1b6464126b5c11ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5569f17f529fd10346ca691a582f1a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b93e00a9cc3c6ea937c6c587abe580f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fef9d4f066439678dcf9e73935433d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d313e963f5afd4511121b3011aa2c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-791d993b170dda54c1f646cc730be410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9817d6c2a44499a793919afdc362415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-430166eda1140532dd1c88ca903c35b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b4df5b01d976649250f6436e21c973&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0256a8b75cb8334fe03b715b6c84c437&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1033809decf9ea155de9688c644d3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e32f71ea37f2011ffa9c3166235ce93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-231d778102a2cbcc7f2f4300f5629d66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6946cf77d89e363da36211d90f9912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405d3a718f7ecf6421ab9b20b50849aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-601d339a4a493a5f03ee5c3181e3905b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8aeb870066721a39cb33b3cacee828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825d31ce533f64fd232a2407d882af7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f012afbc78a585fbfae845130e83a796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3af2defb9bc456081d4547c62ac2dbcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abacff6e2984923123c9fdcc9f5afcb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af8c6d503e4007ddea82e86657430f46</data>
