<node id="[LOCATION] Chicago">
  <data key="d0">[LOCATION] Chicago</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Chicago is the city referenced across the provided descriptions in connection with bodycam footage, reporting, detention-centre context, and multiple Border Patrol-related incidents. It is identified as the location where agents were filmed during Operation Midway Blitz, where use-of-force incidents occurred, and where Judge Ellis’ ruling detailed incidents involving gas and chemical irritants.

Chicago is also the site of the preliminary injunction hearing, the Little Village incident, and an Oct. 23 incident. In addition, it is the city where two agents visible in Campos footage were filmed ten months later.&lt;SEP&gt;City referenced in the ICE operation, protests, and article subject matter.&lt;SEP&gt;City referenced as the broader location for Cicero and Hoffman Estates.&lt;SEP&gt;City named as the broader location for multiple incidents and neighborhoods.&lt;SEP&gt;City referenced in the incident involving Bahena.</data>
