<node id="[PERSON] Gregory Bovino">
  <data key="d0">[PERSON] Gregory Bovino</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Gregory Bovino is a U.S. Customs and Border Protection commander and former Border Patrol Commander at Large. He has been associated with the El Centro sector and identified in footage near EZ-17, where he is described as leading Trump’s immigration raids. He has also been linked to incidents in Chicago and Minneapolis, and at least one description notes that he was seen alongside many agents or near agents on one occasion.

Bovino has additionally been identified as a Border Patrol Commander who was questioned by Judge Ellis over alleged violations of a temporary restraining order. Overall, the descriptions portray Gregory Bovino as a senior Border Patrol figure involved in immigration enforcement operations and related legal scrutiny.</data>
