<node id="[OBJECT] tear gas">
  <data key="d0">[OBJECT] tear gas</data>
  <data key="d1">object</data>
  <data key="d2">Tear gas is a riot control and less-lethal crowd-control chemical used against protesters and referenced in multiple incidents and testimony. In the described material, it is specifically associated with Chicago incidents and with Kristopher Hewson, who used tear gas after warning about deploying the crowd-control agent in Chicago.

The descriptions also note that tear gas was deployed in the fifth shot and that it is referenced in connection with CS. Overall, tear gas is presented as a crowd-control weapon and chemical deployed in multiple incidents, with the available descriptions linking it to both testimony and specific use cases involving protest control.</data>
