<node id="[ORGANIZATION] ICE">
  <data key="d0">[ORGANIZATION] ICE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ICE refers to U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement, a federal immigration agency cited across the descriptions in connection with enforcement actions, policy discussions, and operational incidents. It is identified as the agency operating a processing center, as the subject of protests and an enforcement operation, and as the federal body involved in clashes and in a fatal incident in Minneapolis.

ICE is also referenced in oversight and use-of-force contexts, including a 2021 DHS Office of Inspector General report and DHS policy discussions. The descriptions note that ICE was not required to conduct yearly recertification for PepperBall guns and FN303s, indicating its role in weapons and recertification policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-144039d9b499b5a1b6464126b5c11ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b4df5b01d976649250f6436e21c973&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0256a8b75cb8334fe03b715b6c84c437&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1033809decf9ea155de9688c644d3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63051b407620cc9dc179a3eb02bac5dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8aeb870066721a39cb33b3cacee828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825d31ce533f64fd232a2407d882af7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abacff6e2984923123c9fdcc9f5afcb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af8c6d503e4007ddea82e86657430f46</data>
