<node id="[OBJECT] pepper spray">
  <data key="d0">[OBJECT] pepper spray</data>
  <data key="d1">object</data>
  <data key="d2">pepper spray is a chemical spray commonly used as a riot control and less-lethal crowd-control agent. It is associated with use against protesters, including instances described in Chicago and Evanston, and it is referenced as a weapon in an article, as well as in connection with a Sam’s Club livestream post. One description specifically identifies it as a spray deployed by Kristopher Hewson in Chicago, while another notes it was pointed at protesters in Evanston.

pepper spray is also described as an alternate name for oleoresin capsicum spray, and as a pepper spray formulation containing compounds equivalent to oleoresin capsicum (OC) and PavaPowder. The descriptions collectively link pepper spray to OC-based chemical agents and emphasize its role as a less-lethal chemical spray used for crowd control and protest suppression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-144039d9b499b5a1b6464126b5c11ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d313e963f5afd4511121b3011aa2c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e32f71ea37f2011ffa9c3166235ce93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7672b3b47339e0fa256bbc603183e57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5847b97b78096be5085730e8050c4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405d3a718f7ecf6421ab9b20b50849aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-601d339a4a493a5f03ee5c3181e3905b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddda38fff0b28618245a95601266bd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af8c6d503e4007ddea82e86657430f46</data>
  <data key="d4">raw/84d7e0b9-ebfc-4681-b2ae-7048a4704aa1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;raw/c1731560-2392-47fb-814c-5a1da0d7084b.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;raw/8074ac13-a31c-438f-af03-f65b153c5122.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;raw/3b1a02e9-1614-4381-944c-4fc7c7401511.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1780000496</data>
</node>
